# Execute the current task

Implement the selected story or resolve pending review findings in this repository.

## Workflow and constraints

1. Verify the attached checkout matches `branchName`. If `noBranch=true`, never
   switch/create a branch: report a mismatch. Otherwise use the planned branch,
   creating it from `__BASE_BRANCH__` only when safe. Preserve unrelated user work.
2. Pending `lastReviewFindings` take priority even if every story passes.
   Otherwise implement the active story in the context below.
   Work on one story; when __STORIES_PER_ITERATION__ is greater than 1, you may
   complete that many related stories after verifying their dependencies in the plan.
3. Follow existing code and applicable repository rules. Verify the change with
   relevant checks after the final edit. The orchestrator runs acceptance at the end
   of execute and again before review; that does not replace this story's evidence.
4. Stage only this logical change and commit after its required checks pass, using
   `__COMMIT_MESSAGE__`. Update only verified stories to `passes: true` and record
   concise evidence in their notes. Preserve other plan fields and unrelated stories.
5. Append progress with timestamp, story ID, changes, affected files, commands/results
   and unresolved limitations. Add reusable discoveries to Codebase Patterns; preserve
   previous entries. Put durable repository knowledge in its existing documentation,
   linking it from AGENTS.md when appropriate, without duplicating instruction files.

## Correction findings

Validate each finding against code and requirements. Make focused corrections rather
than reimplementing completed stories. Commit fixes using `__FIX_COMMIT_MESSAGE__`
(or a more specific subject with the same resolved prefix).

Clear `lastReviewFindings` only after every finding is addressed or rejected with
recorded evidence. If work remains, keep the findings and record what remains in
progress. A fresh review still decides whether the corrected work passes.

## Completion and blockers

Emit `<promise>COMPLETE</promise>` only after all stories pass, pending findings have
been addressed, and required verification is complete. Otherwise end normally for
another iteration, or record a non-transient blocker in top-level `lastError` as
`{message, category, at}` with an ISO timestamp. Clear lastError only when its blocker is resolved.

__EXECUTION_SCOPE__ The CLI owns pipeline flags, timestamps and final phase status;
changing these fields in the projection cannot complete review or publication.

